    "background_story": "Jordan was a free-spirited artist who spent his days exploring the city's hidden gems. Among his favorite haunts was a quaint little bookstore tucked away in a quiet alley. The store, named 'Page & Co.', was run by a kind-hearted owner named Sophia, who shared Jordan's passion for literature and music. As he spent more time in the store, Jordan discovered that Sophia was not only a fellow book lover but also a talented musician. He began to attend her intimate concerts, held within the store's walls, and soon found himself smitten with the charming atmosphere and Sophia's soulful voice. Page & Co. became Jordan's favorite refuge, a place where art, music, and literature blended together in perfect harmony.",
